s right we sell shoes we sell  clothes but we don't sell pizza yet and  she's like I know but I heard you all  about the best customer service and the  rep said ok hold on and put us on hold  for two minutes and then came back  listing the five closest places in the  Santa Monica area that we're still open  and delivering pizza at that hour now  well first of all I I hesitated a little  to tell the story because I don't want  all of you to start calling Zappos and  ordering pizza froze but you know  clearly we don't have a process and  procedure for late night drunk pizza  orders but it it just goes back to I  just think it's a fun story to  illustrate that if you get the culture  right then most of the other stuff like  delivering great customer service and  building your brand one story at a time  one phone call at a time just happens  naturally on  you know these types of stories we're  creating at Zappos literally thousands  of thousands of times every single day  and that's how we built our brand over  the years and these are you know  questions that we think about how do we  create more happy memories for customers  and how do we listen more positive  emotions and really were in the memories  and emotions business and stories  business and then we also think about  how do we keep thinking differently and  expanding what business were actually  and how do we think bigger and think  differently and one of my favorite  stories is about Cirque de Soleil where  you know they completely redefine the  circus business prior to the Cirque de  Soleil to have a better circus men more  elephants bigger elephants and the  market research surveys if they did them  would be exiting you know doing exit  polls and they'd be like were the  elephants of sufficient quantity and  sufficient size and you know and then  that that would tell them how to build a  better surface and the surface light  just thought completely you know outside  the box so anyways just wanted to wrap  up 